    {
      "id": "help-long-press",
      "capture": "@window",
      "steps": [
        {
          "open_tab": "image_compare"
        },
        {
          "sleep": 1.5
        },
        {
          "ui_press": {
            "id": "@image_compare.swap",
            "release": false
          }
        },
        {
          "sleep": 0.8
        }
      ],
      "after_capture": [
        {
          "ui_press": {
            "id": "@image_compare.swap",
            "release": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "crop": null,
      "crop_element": {
        "role": "button",
        "label": "Swap Images",
        "pad": 6
      },
      "destination": "src/resources/help/assets/ui/long_press.png",
      "locales": [
        "en"
      ],
      "themes": [
        "dark"
      ],
      "min_size": [
        800,
        500
      ],
      "note": "Hold state of a long-press control: @image_compare.swap is the toolbar button built with long_press=True (src/tabs/image_compare/ui/primitives.py:111-119), i.e. the Swap list control whose long press swaps both lists (comparison.md). The press is parked with ui_press release=false, photographed while held, and released by after_capture. Crop is the button itself (role=button, label from the bound image_compare.swap action); the stronger action the long press would run is not part of the frame."
    },
    {
      "id": "help-paste-overlay",
      "capture": "@screen",
      "steps": [
        {
          "open_tab": "image_compare"
        },
        {
          "sleep": 1.5
        },
        {
          "open_folder": {
            "path": "@samples/singles/sunset",
            "tab": "image_compare",
            "slot": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "sleep": 2.5
        },
        {
          "set_clipboard": "@samples/forest.png"
        },
        {
          "action": "platform.paste_clipboard_image"
        },
        {
          "sleep": 1.5
        }
      ],
      "crop": null,
      "destination": "src/resources/help/assets/platform/paste_overlay.jpg",
      "locales": [
        "en"
      ],
      "themes": [
        "dark"
      ],
      "min_size": [
        1000,
        600
      ],
      "rhi_backend": "vulkan",
      "note": "The direction picker a paste opens: set_clipboard owns the X selection with a demo image, then the platform.paste_clipboard_image action runs the app's own Ctrl+V entry point (it is the keymap default for Ctrl+V, src/ui/actions/platform.py:426-431, and it emits the same ExportPasteImageFromClipboardEvent the canvas Ctrl+V handler emits at events/image_label/keyboard.py:45) so the overlay appears over the loaded session. Captured @window because PasteDirectionOverlay is a window-level in-window overlay (TopLevelInWindowOverlay, parent = main window) and a tab capture never includes a window-level overlay; the overlay itself has no role and no dynamic property, so it is not in ui_elements and has no screen_rect to crop by."
    },
